      "functional_impact_measured": "Surface labeling with a membrane-impermeant HaloTag dye confirmed that the tagged channel reaches the plasma membrane; no electrophysiological functional assay is reported in the ledger clips.",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "rationale": "L3 explicitly names the junction as between S613 and K614 in mouse TRPV3, which is a close ortholog of human TRPV3 (both 790 aa). Python lookup of the human canonical sequence confirms position 613 = P and position 614 = K; the residue identity at 613 differs between species (mouse S, human P) but the position number is identical, placing the junction in the same extracellular S5\u2013S6 loop (human EC3: 610\u2013652). The site is 4 residues from the S5 TM boundary (end at 609) and 40 residues from the S6 TM boundary (start at 653), satisfying the \u22653-residue rule. Because the named residue S613 belongs to mouse and not human, the position is classified as inferred rather than validated. A circularly permuted HaloTag was inserted between residues S613 and K614 of the extracellular S5\u2013S6 loop in full-length, membrane-anchored mouse TRPV3 (mTRPV3), expressed in mammalian cells. The construct was used as a fluorescent reporter of channel subcellular localization and enabled selective labeling of surface-expressed channels with a membrane-impermeant dye.",
