  "literature_notes": "L1, L2, L4, and L5 all describe the same mouse TRPV3 cpHaloTag experiment as L3 but without naming a specific residue; L3 is the single most informative clip and is used as the supporting line. L6\u2013L8 report a dual HA-Strep tag placed at the N-terminus of human TRPV3; the N-terminus falls entirely within the intracellular domain (topology 1\u2013439) and therefore does not qualify as a surface site. L9\u2013L10 report an N-terminal myc tag on mouse TRPV3; same disqualification. L11 reports a C-terminal EGFP on full-length human TRPV3; the C-terminus falls within the intracellular domain (topology 682\u2013790) and does not qualify. No ledger line supports an extracellular insertion other than the S5\u2013S6 loop site at 613|614. Two cysteines (C612, C619) flank the insertion site and may form a disulfide; the mouse paper nonetheless selected and used this junction successfully, so the site is retained with medium confidence.",
